/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (SCoT-based prompting consistently outperformed all other methods on both Gemini 2.5 Pro and GPT-4o-mini. Its structured reasoning, multiple candidate generation, and auto-fix mechanism helped avoid the clause-level errors that affected other approaches. Although Standard and QDecomp variants remained competitive, traditional Chain-of-Thought performed the weakest due to its overly detailed reasoning steps. Overall, our results show that adding structure to the reasoning process makes Text-to-SQL generation more accurate and reliable across different model sizes.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
